      "side": 1,
      "message": "This means you can never target a module to 1.9, which will likely be necessary. Does this really need to change everything that targets 1.9 to 1.11, or should it change the default when unspecified and leave manual selections alone?\n\nThere are only 4 Android.bp files in the tree that currently specify 1.9, and they look like the ones that needed 1.9 when the default was 1.8 (https://cs.android.com/search?q\u003d%22java_version:%20%5C%221.9%5C%22%22).  Those lines should probably be deleted now that 1.9 is the default.",
      "revId": "e40478176cd2d9dad3c4aac051cb4cfde30f1892",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
