      "writtenOn": "2021-12-06T23:00:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that\u0027s right, when the experimental env var is set, 1.11 will be used, even though 1.9 was specified in the module. Though the EXPERIMENTAL_TARGET_JAVA_VERSION_11 flag is not used in any of the current builds, it\u0027s just used to test as we\u0027re preparing for the update to 1.11.\n\nOnce it\u0027s ready for the switch, we\u0027ll remove the code added here, and just use 1.11 for default. In any case, I think that by that time the 1.9 options currently used in Android.bp files will probably be removed, or updated to 1.11.",
      "parentUuid": "20230ea8_cec3e0e3",
      "revId": "e40478176cd2d9dad3c4aac051cb4cfde30f1892",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4af8537_66bd9d93",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 434,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-06T23:18:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But if along the way you find some code that is incompatible with 1.11 you have no way to pin it to 1.9 to unblock moving forward on 1.11.\n\nI\u0027d suggest:\n- remove the no-op java_version: \"1.9\" lines in Android.bp files.\n- when the flag is set only change the default version to 1.11.\n \nThat will give you the same behavior as this CL, but also give you more flexibility to deal with problems that come up later by adding java_language: \"1.9\" to modules that are incompatible with 1.11.",
      "parentUuid": "4d36c813_1e3e9232",
      "revId": "e40478176cd2d9dad3c4aac051cb4cfde30f1892",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
